  "status_text": "Tried for half an hour, on paper: the last sentence the three-gate step needs, that in a cheapest circuit the stray part of one wire is always covered by the vertex's two neighbours. The seat came back suspecting the opposite: nothing about being cheapest forces it, and cutting the stray part away would cost a gate. On the 5-cycle no cheapest circuit carries it, on the 6-cycle the shape never occurs, and the 7-cycle ran past its time limit (computed). So the test goes to the desk: one 10-gate circuit for the 7-cycle with the stray part in it ends the claim.",
